      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ceramic-matrix composite (CMC) pads typically exhibit superior thermal dissipation rates and lower heat-soak susceptibility compared to standard semi-metallic pads during high-speed deceleration. While semi-metallic pads generate intense localized heat that can swell and alter friction coefficients, CMC pads maintain a more stable friction surface due to their high-temperature stability. Consequently, CMC is generally preferred for managing severe thermal gradients on the rotor, as it reduces the risk of cracking or warping the rotor during repeated heavy braking cycles.",
      "source": "target",
