      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The erratic behavior you describe likely stems from thermo-elastic hysteresis and localized melting rather than intrinsic micro-structural instability in the bulk material. As semi-metallic pads heat above ~600°C, organic binders and metal dusts outgas rapidly, forming a lubricating film that causes sudden friction loss. This outgassing acts as a phase-change mechanism where trapped volatiles depressurize the friction surface unpredictably, rather than a failure of the pad's internal grain structure. Switching to CMC resolves this by eliminating the volatile organic binders and stabilizing the friction interface up to 1000°C.",
      "source": "target",
